eople from other ethnic groups. Al-Qaeda has mounted attacks on civilian and military targets of the U.S. and its allies; such as the 1998 U.S. embassy bombings, the USS Cole bombing, and the September 11 attacks. It has been designated a terrorist organization by the United Nations and over two dozen countries around the world.", "newValue": "Al-Qaeda, founded in 1988 by Osama bin Laden during the Soviet-Afghan War, emerged as a prominent pan-Islamist militant organization with a vision to establish a global Islamic caliphate. Its operations and ideology have had far-reaching consequences, particularly in the context of global terrorism and the geopolitical landscape of the Middle East. The group has been responsible for significant terrorist attacks, including the 1998 U.S. embassy bombings in Kenya and Tanzania, the USS Cole bombing in Yemen in 2000, and the September 11 attacks in 2001, which resulted in nearly 3,000 deaths and triggered the U.S.-led invasion of Afghanistan.

